ght, exacerbated by nearly 10% USDA workforce cuts and reduced foreign facility inspections during the previous Trump administration.","shortHeadline":"Beef Industry Issues","topic":"Food Safety","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51951-6a95949a3dd31b629da211e2"},{"title":"Latest 2026 Senate Polls: El-Sayed Leads Rogers By 4 Points In Michigan","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/08/31/latest-2026-senate-polls-el-sayed-leads-rogers-by-4-points-in-michigan/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a7398d78c976550e2cf97e9/960x0.jpg","author":"Sara Dorn","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5010031","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn","authorBio":"Sara Dorn is a Forbes news reporter who covers politics, with a focus on elections and Capitol Hill. She joined Forbes in 2022 and is based in New York. She's covered the 2022 midterms, 2024 presidential campaign, the January 6 House committee investigation, former House Speaker Kevin McCarthy's historic ouster, the 2023 State of the Union Address, former President Donald Trump's federal election interference and classified documents cases and his Manhattan hush money case. Dorn graduated in 2012 from the University of Dayton with a degree in journalism. Prior to joining Forbes, she covered New York City and state politics for the New York Post and City and State magazine. Follow her for updates and analysis on the 2024 presidential race, key Senate and House races and developments in Congress and at the White House.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/63457b718c2404f82daa3149/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1284\u0026cropY1=403\u0026cropY2=1687","authorSlug":"saradorn","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"Republicans face a significant risk of losing their narrow Senate majority in the upcoming November midterm elections, with five of the six seats rated as toss-ups by the Cook Political Report currently held by the GOP. Notably, only one 