,"naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/6117-6a8aa716a628eda2e6c43497"},{"title":"10 Days At The Edge Of The Earth","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/sarahkingdom/2026/08/22/10-days-at-the-edge-of-the-earth/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a89f5a575f835265eae708d/960x0.jpg","author":"Sarah Kingdom","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/7243619","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/sarahkingdom","authorBio":"Sarah Kingdom is a Zambia-based travel writer with over 30 years of experience living, working and exploring across Africa. Born in Australia, she moved to Zambia at the age of 21 and has since made her home on a cattle ranch in the middle of the country. Her writing focuses on luxury and adventure travel, with a particular emphasis on Africa’s wild and lesser-known places, from high-end safaris to off-the-grid trekking. Sarah is a regular contributor to leading publications including Africa Geographic, Travel Africa, Getaway, The Outdoor Journal and Adventure.com. Whether profiling conservation-led lodges or exploring the cultural heart of remote communities, she brings her knowledge of the continent and a storyteller’s eye to every assignment. You can follow her travels on IG @sarah_kingdom_travels.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/686e947b9cd0ee677e1b3180/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1500\u0026cropY1=137\u0026cropY2=1637","authorSlug":"sarahkingdom","authorType":"Contributor","summary":"An expedition to Svalbard aboard the MV Freya, a 12-guest ship from Secret Atlas, is an incredible and immersive Arctic experience under the perpetual \"midnight sun.\" The journey provides unique wildlife encounters, including a polar bears, walruses, and seals. Svalbard's 24-hour daylight allows for flexible exploration of its remote landscapes, from glaciers to sea ice. The small ship means a personal experience, allowing guests to observe wildlife closely and responsibly. Guests participate in beach clean-ups, confronting the reality of marine debris and its threat to Arctic species. The expedition underscores that climate change poses a significant threat, by altering the Arctic's very structure. The experience emphasizes that responsible tourism in the High Arctic is not just about witnessing its wonders, but understanding its vulnerabilities and the urgent need for attention to its changing state.","shortHeadline":"Extreme Expeditions","topic":"Travel","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/52973-6a89f049d7c252488356b935"}],"audioUrl":"https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/1OSCLfGZ-3GQxW5ax.m4a","mediaId":"1OSCLfGZ","audioDurationS":296,"audioFormat":"audio/mp4","generatedAt":"2026-08-23T08:30:37-05:00"},{"id":"BRIEF-2026-08-22-MORNING","cadence":"morning","date":"2026-08-22","script":"You're listening to The Daily Brief, your essential news update from Forbes. It's Saturday, August 22. Today, we're highlighting the key stories covering Trade Policy, Celebrity Marketing, and a closer look at Innovation.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nLeading off with, Trump announces 90-day tariff relief for ground beef imports as costs soar. Sara Dorn has been tracking this development and reports that\n\nPresident Donald Trump announced a 90-day tariff exemption for certain ground beef products, allowing up to 300,000 metric tons to be imported without out-of-quota tariffs. He stated this beef would be sold at 25% below current market prices. This move comes as Trump faces low approval ratings on his economic handling and the rising cost of living, key issues for voters ahead of the 2026 midterm elections. Polls indicate a majority of registered voters feel financially worse off during his second term and trust Democrats more on inflation. Ground beef prices have soared to record highs, reaching $6.89 per pound in July, with the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics reporting an average of $13.06 per pound, attributed to a cattle shortage. The specifics of the exempted products remain unclear. This action follows a previous delay in a planned beef import suspension in May, which had drawn concerns from ranchers. Earlier this year, Trump also increased Argentine beef import quotas for lean trimmings, a decision that also angered some cattle ranchers.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nRead the full report on that story at Forbes.com. Moving now to, Hailey bieber spotted wearing skylrk’s wired earbuds as the brand soft-launches its audio expansion, a story that's currently shaping the landscape in Celebrity Marketing.\n\nHailey Bieber was photographed wearing unreleased wired earbuds from SKYLRK Audio, Justin Bieber’s upcoming tech brand. These sightings confirm SKYLRK's expansion from its fashion and lifestyle origins into consumer electronics. Justin Bieber first teased SKYLRK Audio in June 2026, showcasing retro-futurist speakers, headphones, and vibrant, Y2K-inspired earbuds. Hailey's public appearances serve as a strategic \"soft launch,\" generating organic visibility and leveraging her cultural influence. The wired earbuds are a notable choice, aligning with a current fashion trend valuing their aesthetic and reliability. This move positions SKYLRK to blend fashion and audio, maintaining the brand's consistent visual identity. Technical specs, pricing, and release dates remain undisclosed, yet these high-profile sightings create buzz. Hailey's active involvement reinforces her role beyond a muse, shaping SKYLRK's direction and complementing her Rhode brand. Success hinges on product quality and market reception, but this initial visibility is a vital first step.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nTo finish today's update, we're turning to, Jeremy matlow on designing a better future with a new style of innovation. This headline is generating significant interest within Innovation.\n\nPolitical messaging has evolved significantly, from 1948's \"Dew it with Dewey\" tees to modern campaign buttons, reflecting technological shifts and a growing public sophistication. Tallahassee mayoral candidate Jeremy Matlow, a current city commissioner, embodies this evolution, prioritizing authenticity over curated political images. He first ran in 2018, motivated by national unrest and local corruption, aiming to make government serve everyday people. Matlow believes in being true to himself, dressing for comfort while engaging with constituents, and challenging the traditional \"pedestal\" view of politicians. His platform focuses on rebuilding city government to deliver for the public, not entrenched interests. Key proposals include aggressive municipal housing development, targeting 500 units in four years, lowering utility costs, investing in underserved neighborhoods, and protecting natural spaces. Matlow also champions the arts, advocating for local funding and streamlined permitting to foster a vibrant cultural scene, envisioning Tallahassee as a \"south by southeast\" destination. He remains optimistic about the community's resilience and its potential for transformational change through this election.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nThat wraps up this edition of The Daily Brief. Be sure to check back tomorrow for our next update. Thanks for listening.","scriptTemplateId":1,"articles":[{"title":"Trump Announces 90-Day Tariff Relief For Ground Beef Imports As Costs Soar","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/08/21/trump-announces-90-day-tariff-relief-for-ground-beef-imports-as-costs-soar/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a8858ff8fa3b55406f43ca9/960x0.jpg","author":"Sara Dorn","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5010031","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn","authorBio":"Sara Dorn is a Forbes news reporter who covers politics, with a focus on elections and Capitol Hill. She joined Forbes in 2022 and is based in New York. She's covered the 2022 midterms, 2024 presidential campaign, the January 6 House committee investigation, former House Speaker Kevin McCarthy's historic ouster, the 2023 State of the Union Address, former President Donald Trump's federal election interference and classified documents cases and his Manhattan hush money case. Dorn graduated in 2012 from the University of Dayton with a degree in journalism. Prior to joining Forbes, she covered New York City and state politics for the New York Post and City and State magazine. Follow her for updates and analysis on the 2024 presidential race, key Senate and House races and developments in Congress and at the White House.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/63457b718c2404f82daa3149/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1284\u0026cropY1=403\u0026cropY2=1687","authorSlug":"saradorn","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"President Donald Trump announced a 90-day tariff exemption for certain ground beef products, allowing up to 300,000 metric tons to be imported without out-of-quota tariffs. He stated this beef would be sold at 25% below current market prices. This move comes as Trump faces low approval ratings on his economic handling and the rising cost of living, key issues for voters ahead of the 2026 midterm elections. Polls indicate a majority of registered voters feel financially worse off during his second term and trust Democrats more on inflation. Ground beef prices have soared to record highs, reaching $6.89 per pound in July, with the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics reporting an average of $13.06 per pound, attributed to a cattle shortage. The specifics of the exempted products remain unclear. This action follows a previous delay in a planned beef import suspension in May, which had drawn concerns from ranchers. Earlier this year, Trump also increased Argentine beef import quotas for lean trimmings, a decision that also angered some cattle ranchers.","shortHeadline":"Beef Import Tariffs","topic":"Trade Policy","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51554-6a8858bd24c0ce5091739916"},{"title":"Hailey Bieber Spotted Wearing Skylrk’s Wired Earbuds As The Brand Soft-Launches Its Audio Expansion","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/tanyaakim/2026/08/21/hailey-bieber-spotted-wearing-skylrks-wired-earbuds-as-the-brand-soft-launches-its-audio-expansion/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a885de3759c70f3cb198841/960x0.jpg","author":"Tanya Akim","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5002087","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/tanyaakim","authorBio":"Tanya Akim is a New York City \u0026 Los Angeles-based journalist covering beauty, fashion, wellness, and culture. Additional bylines include Architectural Digest, Bustle, Byrdie, Cosmopolitan, Coveteur, The Cut, Eater, L’Officiel, Marie Claire, The New York Times, V Magazine, Well+Good, and more. She’s not on social media and never has been. Questions or comments? Email: ta@tanyaakim.com","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/5f49540c61c17ae223b82917/400x0.jpg?cropX1=204\u0026cropX2=960\u0026cropY1=693\u0026cropY2=1449","authorSlug":"tanyaakim","authorType":"Contributor","summary":"Hailey Bieber was photographed wearing unreleased wired earbuds from SKYLRK Audio, Justin Bieber’s upcoming tech brand. These sightings confirm SKYLRK's expansion from its fashion and lifestyle origins into consumer electronics. Justin Bieber first teased SKYLRK Audio in June 2026, showcasing retro-futurist speakers, headphones, and vibrant, Y2K-inspired earbuds. Hailey's public appearances serve as a strategic \"soft launch,\" generating organic visibility and leveraging her cultural influence. The wired earbuds are a notable choice, aligning with a current fashion trend valuing their aesthetic and reliability. This move positions SKYLRK to blend fashion and audio, maintaining the brand's consistent visual identity. Technical specs, pricing, and release dates remain undisclosed, yet these high-profile sightings create buzz. Hailey's active involvement reinforces her role beyond a muse, shaping SKYLRK's direction and complementing her Rhode brand. Success hinges on product quality and market reception, but this initial visibility is a vital first step.","shortHeadline":"Celebrity Product Placements","topic":"Celebrity Marketing","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/50743-6a885994a4cc22bd7f33542d"},{"title":"Jeremy Matlow On Designing A Better Future With A New Style Of Innovation","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/rachelelspethgross/2026/08/21/jeremy-matlow-on-designing-a-better-future-with-a-new-style-of-innovation/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a87c92930c1c20897427597/960x0.jpg","author":"Rachel Elspeth Gross","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/7238551","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/rachelelspethgross","authorBio":"I am a fashion writer and historian who is passionate about the stories behind clothing and costume. I write in-depth articles about costume design and speak with the greatest people working in that field, like Oscar-winning designers Jenny Beavan, Ruth E. Carter, and Deborah L. Scott. My fashion writing includes interviews with a wide range of international talent including Lilia Litkovska, and Caroline Vazzana, and Tinka Weener. I love to support the work of those who are preserving fashion history, including the best fashion museums and schools in the world, and I make a point of highlighting the excellent work of people like Keli Goff, Dr. Stephanie Lake, and Dr. Elizabeth Way. You can find more of my work on Instagram and on my Yahoo Creators page.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/65775f78632cb2f32c29b4e4/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1365\u0026cropY1=0\u0026cropY2=1364","authorSlug":"rachelelspethgross","authorType":"Contributor","summary":"Political messaging has evolved significantly, from 1948's \"Dew it with Dewey\" tees to modern campaign buttons, reflecting technological shifts and a growing public sophistication. Tallahassee mayoral candidate Jeremy Matlow, a current city commissioner, embodies this evolution, prioritizing authenticity over curated political images. He first ran in 2018, motivated by national unrest and local corruption, aiming to make government serve everyday people. Matlow believes in being true to himself, dressing for comfort while engaging with constituents, and challenging the traditional \"pedestal\" view of politicians. His platform focuses on rebuilding city government to deliver for the public, not entrenched interests. Key proposals include aggressive municipal housing development, targeting 500 units in four years, lowering utility costs, investing in underserved neighborhoods, and protecting natural spaces. Matlow also champions the arts, advocating for local funding and streamlined permitting to foster a vibrant cultural scene, envisioning Tallahassee as a \"south by southeast\" destination. He remains optimistic about the community's resilience and its potential for transformational change through this election.","shortHeadline":"Innovative Design Futures","topic":"Innovation","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/52270-6a7cd56ddcbb9c698b3156f7"}],"audioUrl":"https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/uJoikQPF-3GQxW5ax.m4a","mediaId":"uJoikQPF","audioDurationS":289,"audioFormat":"audio/mp4","generatedAt":"2026-08-22T08:30:39-05:00"},{"id":"BRIEF-2026-08-21-MORNING","cadence":"morning","date":"2026-08-21","script":"Welcome to The Daily Brief, the essential news digest from the Forbes newsroom. It's Friday, August 21. Today, we're exploring the stories shaping the global conversation—from the latest in Politics and Media to a deep dive into Elections.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nWe begin with a look at, Ossoff says MAGA ‘melt down’ over his natalie harp comments has been ‘amazing’: ‘the truth hurts’. Sara Dorn has been following this story and reports that\n\nSenator Jon Ossoff, D-Ga., has staunchly defended his recent remarks concerning Trump aide Natalie Harp, accusing the White House of a \"melt down\" over his comments. Ossoff's controversial statement, made during a campaign rally, alluded to Trump's desire to \"build his ballroom and travel with Natalie on their apparently defenseless flying palace gifted by the emir of Qatar,\" referencing Harp's reported presence on a secret flight with Trump. The senator has repeatedly doubled down, asserting that White House staffers are \"adults, public officials paid by the taxpayer, with immense power in positions of public trust,\" and that \"no one cares about their feelings\" regarding their role in facilitating Trump's decisions. He clarified his intent was to inform Georgians about the administration, suggesting \"the truth hurts\" the White House. The comments have drawn intense blowback from President Trump and his allies, with Trump reviving his \"Pee-wee Herman\" nickname for Ossoff, and White House figures like Steven Cheung calling Ossoff \"a miserable person.\" Even some on the left, including Democratic strategist David Axelrod, have questioned if Ossoff's specific mention of Harp was \"gratuitous and unnecessary,\" distracting from his broader message, despite its viral impact. Harp, known as Trump's \"human printer\" for her extreme loyalty and role in providing him with information, has been a central figure in this political firestorm.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou can find the full analysis of that story at Forbes.com. Now, we're turning our attention to, Sean duffy’s road trip series launches with a whimper—and lots of questions, a development that could have a lasting impact on Media.\n\nTransportation Secretary Sean Duffy's \"Great American Road Trip\" reality show, featuring his family of 11, finally launched on YouTube this week, despite its original aim to inspire summer travel. The five-part series, filmed between September 2025 and April 2026, debuted after most U.S. schoolchildren had already returned to class, rendering its summer-focused message largely irrelevant. The show has garnered minimal viewership, with just over 5,100 views by Thursday morning. Critics have labeled the project an \"ethical catastrophe,\" pointing out that Duffy accepted corporate-sponsored perks, including flights and luxury accommodations, from companies his department regulates. Sponsors like Boeing, Toyota, and Shell, who contributed up to $1 million each, collectively spent over $100 million lobbying Congress last year. Democratic senators have called for an investigation into potential misconduct, citing concerns about Duffy accepting gifts from regulated entities.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nRounding out today's briefing, we look at, Lindell says he’ll pay for recount after losing minnesota race—as trump stays silent. This story is currently at the center of the conversation in Elections.\n\nMyPillow founder Mike Lindell lost the Minnesota GOP gubernatorial primary to House Speaker Lisa Demuth, who secured 43.6% of the vote. Lindell, a prominent promoter of 2020 election fraud claims, finished second with 32.3%. Despite the Associated Press calling the race, Lindell refused to concede, citing unproven \"anomalies.\" His candidacy was notably backed by former President Donald Trump, who praised Lindell's fight for \"free and fair Elections.\" This defeat adds Lindell to a growing list of Trump-endorsed candidates failing in primaries. In the Democratic primary, Senator Amy Klobuchar overwhelmingly won with 89.6%, holding a strong general election lead. Lindell's campaign faced controversies, including residency questions. He also faced a probable campaign law violation for distributing \"Mike Lindell for Governor\" pillows. Furthermore, he recently settled a $1 billion defamation lawsuit with Dominion Voting Systems over his false 2020 election claims.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou've reached the end of this Daily Brief. Tune in again for tomorrow's updates. Thanks for joining us.","scriptTemplateId