ntage bar books in the process, and tried in vain to impress dates by making them obscure cocktails with rye whiskey. In 2007, he left music retail behind and started writing about bars and booze for a host of publications, including Robb Report, Whisky Advocate, HuffPost and Alcohol Professor. Tasting notes are important, of course, but what he really loves is telling the stories behind the stuff he's drinking.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/63851d8c516466c478a067da/400x0.jpg?cropX1=464\u0026cropX2=2352\u0026cropY1=24\u0026cropY2=1912","authorSlug":"tonysachs","authorType":"Contributor","summary":"A remarkable collection of rare, decades-old single malt Scotch whiskies, discovered in an Italian warehouse, is now available at Collezione New York. These \"new old stock\" bottles, some dating back over half a century, were part of the forgotten inventory of Trattoria Cantarelli, a legendary two-Michelin-star Italian restaurant that closed in 1982. Italy played a pivotal role in the early appreciation of single malts in the 1960s and 70s, with pioneering importers fostering a market when the spirit was still a niche. Stefano Pileggi, Collezione's owner and a former Macallan collector, unearthed this extraordinary find through his connections within the Italian whisky community. The collection boasts pristine bottles of Highland Park, Ardbeg, Macallan-Glenlivet, high-proof Clynelish, and many more. Pileggi emphasizes the unique provenance and condition, offering collectors an unparalleled experience beyond typical auctions, while honoring the legacy of Cantarelli and Italy's foresight in whisky appreciation.","shortHeadline":"Rare Whisky Finds","topic":"Spirits","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51586-6a78eeb80d4db1792e8b7380"},{"title":"A Leader’s Guide To Agentic Governance","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/ceo/2026/08/17/a-leaders-guide-to-agentic-governance/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a8337f411