their daughter in documents Miller released to support his innocence claims. Additionally, the House Ethics Committee announced an investigation into Miller, a probe he had requested himself to clear his name amidst the allegations.","shortHeadline":"Campaign Disputes","topic":"Political Campaigns","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51554-6a722c09cbe9922b9fc4b468"}],"audioUrl":"https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/JNbjrbSW-3GQxW5ax.m4a","mediaId":"JNbjrbSW","audioDurationS":275,"audioFormat":"audio/mp4","generatedAt":"2026-08-07T06:30:38-05:00"},{"id":"BRIEF-2026-08-06-MORNING","cadence":"morning","date":"2026-08-06","script":"Welcome to The Daily Brief, the essential news digest from the Forbes newsroom. It's Thursday, August 6. Today, we're exploring the stories shaping the global conversation—from the latest in US Elections and Interior Design to a deep dive into Fine Spirits.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nWe begin with a look at, Establishment democrats line up behind progressive el-sayed after tight race divided party. Sara Dorn has been following this story and reports that\n\nAbdul El-Sayed narrowly clinched Michigan's Democratic Senate nomination, quickly uniting centrist Democrats, including primary opponent Rep. Haley Stevens, Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer, and Gov. Gretchen Whitmer. They pledged support against Republican Mike Rogers, aiming to check Donald Trump and flip the Senate. Still, some party division emerged, with Sen. John Fetterman downplaying El-Sayed's slim victory. President Trump and allies immediately attacked El-Sayed's progressive views, labeling him a \"Communist loser\" and \"radical anti-Israel\" to push their narrative of a far-left Democratic Party and boost Rogers, whom Trump called an easier opponent. El-Sayed, a progressive endorsed by figures like Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, defended his commitment to Jewish safety while maintaining his stance on U.S. aid to Israel and Gaza, rejecting antisemitism claims. Pro-Israel groups, previously backing Stevens, indicated they would now support Rogers. El-Sayed's tight win, despite earlier double-digit poll leads, signifies another high-profile progressive primary success this cycle.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou can find the full analysis of that story at Forbes.com. Now, we're turning our attention to, Valspar kicks off 2027 color of the year season with ‘cottage door’, a development that could have a lasting impact on Interior Design.\n\nValspar Paints has launched the 2027 Color of the Year season, naming Cottage Door (8004-38E) as its selection. This mid-tone neutral blue is described as seductively serene, offering calm and an antidote to constant stimulation. Valspar's director, Sue Kim, noted its all-over neutrality, even using it in her bedroom for a cozy, anchored feel. Blue hues are a strong trend, appearing in 2026 reports from Houzz and WGSN/Coloro, which picked \"Luminous Blue\" for 2027. Major brands like Glidden, Sherwin-Williams, and Benjamin Moore have also recently chosen blue shades. Valspar itself previously selected Encore (2025) and Renew Blue, prior to its 2026 choice of Warm Eucalyptus.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nRounding out today's briefing, we look at, Top islay and campbeltown scotch whisky, from the global spirits masters. This story is currently at the center of the conversation in Fine Spirits.\n\nCampbeltown and Islay, despite their modest whisky output, consistently produce some of Scotland's most highly regarded single malts, a reputation strongly reinforced at the 2025 Global Spirits Masters. Campbeltown's Glen Scotia impressed across its core range and limited editions, earning a prestigious Tastemaster Award for its 2026 Malts Festival Edition, alongside Master Medals for its Harbor, 12-Year-Old, and 15-Year-Old expressions, all showcasing elegant maritime character. Islay's Kilchoman and the iconic Lagavulin also secured Master Medals, demonstrating the enduring appeal of expertly balanced peat smoke, coastal influence, and long maturation. Kilchoman's Rockside 11 Years Old highlighted its unique farm-to-bottle style, while Lagavulin 16-Year-Old exemplified its rich peat smoke and maritime elegance. These award-winning whiskies underscore the individuality and world-class quality defining Scotland's western whisky regions. Glen Scotia's performance confirms its growing reputation for refined maritime malts, while Kilchoman and Lagavulin solidify Islay's status as the home of Scotland's most expressive peated whiskies, showcasing diverse and characterful styles.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou've reached the end of this Daily Brief. Tune in again for tomorrow's updates. Thanks for joining us.","scriptTemplateId":0,"articles":[{"title":"Establishment Democrats Line Up Behind Progressive El-Sayed After Tight Race Divided Party","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn/2026/08/05/establishment-democrats-line-up-behind-progressive-el-sayed-after-tight-race-divided-party/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a7398d78c976550e2cf97e9/960x0.jpg","author":"Sara Dorn","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/5010031","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/saradorn","authorBio":"Sara Dorn is a Forbes news reporter who covers politics, with a focus on elections and Capitol Hill. She joined Forbes in 2022 and is based in New York. She's covered the 2022 midterms, 2024 presidential campaign, the January 6 House committee investigation, former House Speaker Kevin McCarthy's historic ouster, the 2023 State of the Union Address, former President Donald Trump's federal election interference and classified documents cases and his Manhattan hush money case. Dorn graduated in 2012 from the University of Dayton with a degree in journalism. Prior to joining Forbes, she covered New York City and state politics for the New York Post and City and State magazine. Follow her for updates and analysis on the 2024 presidential race, key Senate and House races and developments in Congress and at the White House.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/63457b718c2404f82daa3149/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1284\u0026cropY1=403\u0026cropY2=1687","authorSlug":"saradorn","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"Abdul El-Sayed narrowly clinched Michigan's Democratic Senate nomination, quickly uniting centrist Democrats, including primary opponent Rep. Haley Stevens, Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer, and Gov. Gretchen Whitmer. They pledged support against Republican Mike Rogers, aiming to check Donald Trump and flip the Senate. Still, some party division emerged, with Sen. John Fetterman downplaying El-Sayed's slim victory. President Trump and allies immediately attacked El-Sayed's progressive views, labeling him a \"Communist loser\" and \"radical anti-Israel\" to push their narrative of a far-left Democratic Party and boost Rogers, whom Trump called an easier opponent. El-Sayed, a progressive endorsed by figures like Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, defended his commitment to Jewish safety while maintaining his stance on U.S. aid to Israel and Gaza, rejecting antisemitism claims. Pro-Israel groups, previously backing Stevens, indicated they would now support Rogers. El-Sayed's tight win, despite earlier double-digit poll leads, signifies another high-profile progressive primary success this cycle.","shortHeadline":"Democratic Party Unity","topic":"US Elections","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51554-6a73989c0a498617335160f4"},{"title":"Valspar Kicks Off 2027 Color Of The Year Season With ‘Cottage Door’","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/rdaniel-foster/2026/08/05/valspar-kicks-off-2027-color-of-the-year-season-with-cottage-door/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a72b33b1419b494c1d17944/960x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1200\u0026cropY1=41\u0026cropY2=717","author":"R. Daniel Foster","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/7241316","auth