ed himself to clear his name amidst the allegations.","shortHeadline":"Political Accusations","topic":"Politics","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/51554-6a722c09cbe9922b9fc4b468"},{"title":"Sean Duffy’s Road Trip Sponsors Spent $100 Million Lobbying Congress Last Year","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/suzannerowankelleher/2026/08/04/sean-duffy-road-trip-sponsors-spent-100-million-lobbying-congress-2025/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a72117a8412300813989dd4/960x0.jpg","author":"Suzanne Rowan Kelleher","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/3340630","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/suzannerowankelleher/","authorBio":"Suzanne Rowan Kelleher covers travel for Forbes. Follow her on Bluesky @srkelleher.","authorAvatar":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/601b7235b35a3ce5939c28fe/400x0.jpg?cropX1=0\u0026cropX2=1080\u0026cropY1=0\u0026cropY2=1080","authorSlug":"suzannerowankelleher","authorType":"Forbes Staff","summary":"Sean Duffy's \"The Great American Road Trip\" YouTube series, intended to inspire travel for America's 250th anniversary, remains unreleased despite a promoted June launch. Corporate sponsors, including Boeing and Toyota who each contributed $1 million, collectively spent an estimated $5 million on the project. These same companies, however, spent over $100 million lobbying Congress in 2025. The delay has drawn critics who highlight that many sponsors are regulated by Duffy's Department of Transportation, raising concerns about potential conflicts of interest and corporate influence.","shortHeadline":"Lobbying Expenditures","topic":"Lobbying","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/7082-6a7208670a49861733516094"},{"title":"How A Village Of 66 In Spain Is Preparing For The Eclipse — By Closing Its Mountain","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/jamiecartereurope/2026/08/04/how-a-village-of-66-in-spain-is-preparing-for-the-eclipse---by-closing-its-mountain/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com