who covers travel, with a focus on luxury properties and experiences and singular destinations. A contributor since 2014, she’s written about Italy’s best escapes, from glamorous Lake Garda getaways to Sicily’s top foodie vacations, as well as Africa’s most rewarding safaris. She previously covered the business of luxury–from Italian racing rivals to solo exploring on the Great Barrier Reef–as an international reporter at Forbes from 1998 to 2005. Follow Kirkman for the latest news from the world’s leading hoteliers, the hottest openings both stateside and abroad, and emerging travel trends to watch.","authorAvatar":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/779137653ab405614cdc7bc78da8e773?s=400\u0026d=mm\u0026r=g","authorSlug":"alexandrakirkman","authorType":"Contributor","summary":"The Sheraton Stockholm has re-emerged as a premier Nordic destination after a $45 million overhaul, aiming to reinvent the hotel with a lifestyle soul. Located on the waterfront between the Old Town and the modern city center, its 463 spacious rooms boast modern Scandinavian design and locally sourced amenities, while some offer stunning Lake Mälaren views. General Manager Elin Roquet emphasizes blending reliability and warmth with a contemporary feel, reflecting Stockholm's natural beauty. Public spaces include Sally's, a buzzing lobby bar with inventive cocktails, and Mr. Bronck, a lively steakhouse. A wellness center offers cutting-edge fitness and biohacking therapies like cryotherapy for guests and locals. Nearly 10,000 square feet of event space accommodates diverse gatherings, while the concierge team curates insider itineraries, guiding guests to cultural highlights like Fotografiska and Moderna Museet. Shopping options range from SoFo's design district to luxury brands in Bibliotekstan. Nearby, the vibrant G.A.T. bistro offers elevated comfort food and a lively atmosphere.","shortHeadline":"Hotel Renovations","topic":"Hospitality","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/3515-6a63a25f8bd