omeownership alongside lifestyle and affordability. The result is a broader definition of what makes a place worth calling home—and what it may truly cost over time.","shortHeadline":"Climate Migration Trends","topic":"Real Estate","naturalId":"blogAndPostId/blog/post/4251-6a71251592b6a91dae58f74b"}],"audioUrl":"https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/JdHjqWGy-3GQxW5ax.m4a","mediaId":"JdHjqWGy","audioDurationS":227,"audioFormat":"audio/mp4","generatedAt":"2026-08-04T06:30:53-05:00"},{"id":"BRIEF-2026-08-01-MORNING","cadence":"morning","date":"2026-08-01","script":"Welcome to The Daily Brief, the essential news digest from the Forbes newsroom. It's Saturday, August 1. Today, we're exploring the stories shaping the global conversation—from the latest in Comics and Travel to a deep dive into Beauty.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nWe begin with a look at, Seeing ‘spider-man: brand new day’? here’s what you need to know. Dani Di Placido has been following this story and reports that\n\nSpider-Man: Brand New Day finds Peter Parker navigating a world where everyone, including his closest friends, has forgotten him due to Doctor Strange's memory-wiping spell in No Way Home. This profound consequence has forced Peter to mature, transforming him from a Stark-reliant youth into a self-made, solitary crimefighter. The narrative also features an unexpected alliance between Spider-Man and The Punisher, Frank Castle. Despite their stark moral differences, Frank owes Spider-Man a debt. Furthermore, the Department of Damage Control reappears, continuing its mission to clean up superhero battle sites and repurpose alien technology. Finally, Bruce Banner, now seemingly in control of the Hulk via a wrist inhibitor and working as a university professor, makes an appearance. Though he doesn't remember Peter, his tech inspires Peter's own inventions, setting the stage for the inevitable re-emergence of the Hulk.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou can find the full analysis of that story at Forbes.com. Now, we're turning our attention to, 5 unique attractions for families in halifax, nova scotia, a development that could have a lasting impact on Travel.\n\nHalifax, Nova Scotia, emerges as an ideal family travel destination, boasting a compact, walkable downtown and friendly locals. The city offers a wealth of engaging activities, from hands-on learning to outdoor adventures, ensuring entertainment for all ages. A highlight is the iconic Harbour Hopper, an amphibious vehicle providing a unique tour of the downtown and harbour, famously splashing from land into the water. The Halifax Central Library impresses with its distinctive book-stack architecture, a vast children's section, and a rooftop offering superb city views. Within the Discovery Centre, the Dome Theatre captivates with live star viewings and family-friendly documentaries. For aviation enthusiasts, the Atlantic Canada Aviation Museum, a short drive away, displays vintage aircraft and artifacts crucial to Canadian aviation history. History and nature converge at the York Redoubt National Historic Site. This military fort overlooks the harbour entrance, featuring ancient fortifications, historical items, and unparalleled ocean vistas.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nRounding out today's briefing, we look at, This non-invasive treatment lifts and smooths skin with no downtime—even in summer. This story is currently at the center of the conversation in Beauty.\n\nSofwave is a non-invasive skin-tightening device using high-frequency ultrasound to lift and firm skin on the face, neck and body. It stands out for its zero downtime, making it popular even in summer, as it doesn't break the skin barrier and keeps the surface cool despite internal heating, eliminating sun exposure risks. Patients can immediately resume normal activities. Sofwave stimulates collagen, elastin and hyaluronic acid, improving firmness, reducing fine lines and addressing crepey skin and acne scars without fat loss or nerve damage. Typically, one treatment per year is recommended, often integrated into a comprehensive anti-aging regimen alongside other procedures, even on the same day. Experts suggest starting in the late 30s or early 40s to proactively combat collagen loss and maintain skin quality. Results, including lifting and tightening, become visible over 8-12 weeks as collagen builds, lasting about a year. While not painless—patients may experience a \"hot pinch\" during treatment, managed with cooling or numbing cream—the discomfort is temporary, and the results are consistent and long-lasting across all skin types.\n\n\u003cbreak time=\"1.12s\"/\u003e\n\nYou've reached the end of this Daily Brief. Tune in again for tomorrow's updates. Thanks for joining us.","scriptTemplateId":0,"articles":[{"title":"Seeing ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’? Here’s What You Need To Know","url":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/danidiplacido/2026/07/31/seeing-spider-man-brand-new-day-heres-what-you-need-to-know/","image":"https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/imageserve/6a6cdf69c7df6ee014d7107e/960x0.jpg?cropX1=141\u0026cropX2=1715\u0026cropY1=27\u0026cropY2=912","author":"Dani Di Placido","authorNaturalId":"blogAuthorId/blog/author/2014195","authorUrl":"http://www.forbes.com/sites/danidiplacido/","authorBio":"Dani Di Placido has been writing about film, television, and internet culture for Forbes for 8 years. Di Placido covers TikTok and Twitter trends, breaking down interesting conversations and controversies surrounding celebrities and the entertainment industry, focusing on fantasy and sci-fi stories such as Star Wars and House of the Dragon. Di Placido has delved into the meaning of the Oscar-winning film Parasite and explained the origin of popular internet memes, such as the Sigma Male and the Backrooms. Follow Di Placido for more meme explainers, television reviews, film theories and deep dives into digital culture.","authorAvatar":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d772833b74